mkn.ram
===

C++ Remote Applications Management

Convenience library providing cross platform http/https services

How to use:
view test/usage.cpp

License: BSD

Switches - OSX is considered BSD for swiches unless otherwise noted
 
Key             MKN_RAM_TCP_BIND_SOCKTOPTS
Type            text
Default         SO_REUSEADDR
OS              nix/bsd
Description
    Socket options to use on bind

Key             MKN_RAM_HTTPS_CLIENT_METHOD
Type            text
Default         TLS_client_method
OS              nix/bsd
Description
    Method to tell SSL server what method is wanted

Key             MKN_RAM_HTTPS_SERVER_METHOD
Type            text
Default         TLS_server_method
OS              nix/bsd
Description
    Method to tell SSL client is in use


Key             MKN_RAM_HTTPS_METHOD
Type            text
Default         TLS
OS              nix/bsd
Description
    Convenience macro, if MKN_RAM_HTTPS_CLIENT_METHOD and MKN_RAM_HTTPS_SERVER_METHOD are not defined, it is used as the prefix for both i.e.:
    -DMKN_RAM_HTTPS_METHOD=TLS
    -DMKN_RAM_HTTPS_METHOD=TLSv1_2

